<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Sudan: One year after the fall of El-Fasher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebab9d0844292ecfe4adb8b14b5eeef75d22cf507e2a1db1a974380b2fa79cb</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:46:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher--874d8fa8f1e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher" /><summary type="html">It has been one year since the fall of El-Fasher in Sudan, a city in North Darfur, which was captured by the Rapid Support Forces. At least 6,000 civilians were killed by rebel troops as they entered this strategic city.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications after recent unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28c76d9eb3a3341938948570d668dfbc2c933d638a4e98b0a987d608c67a1bd1</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:37:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest--7a8cca00906a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest" /><summary type="html">Tensions in South Africa over anti-migrant protests have left in limbo many who were counting on following the rules to sort out their paperwork and status in the country. Calls for a crackdown on foreigners, particularly undocumented migrants, have sometimes spiralled into murder. In response to the unrest, the government suspended the asylum application process.</summary></entry><entry><title>Algeria to deploy army units to Niger to protect economic interests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f8048bbc95d6b883645d75f3da7850da44966c4e6e6b56ee47ff30acca9a992</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:28:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests--dda1a7fe9e79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests" /><summary type="html">Algeria will send army units to Niger to ​protect energy and economic interests, according to a statement from the presidency on Monday (October 26). Algeria's Parliament held an emergency vote on Sunday on what would be Algeria's first such foreign mission since 1973.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chad hosts hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees as regional humanitarian crisis extends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbf592c7c74f85478a9377861ac9089f543ce4ef0b461be895cafcabe8a5d653</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:13:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-exten--ea71b37e071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-extends" /><summary type="html">Sudan’s war is spilling over into Chad. A drone strike killed at least four people last week in the border town of Bamina, and hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees have crossed over in search of safety. Many of those who survived the massacre in El Fasher are still deeply traumatised. FRANCE 24's correspondent Harold Girard has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>The fall of Sudan's El-Fasher, one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d11b5fc92914f30463c39dbf0758af3c08720e5f7be3bc95ea5e6774f1df8601</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:26:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on--b474e4157040.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: 15 military officials in Sudan are sanctioned by the UK over the brutality and abuse of civilians during the fall of El-Fasher. Also, ⁠Algeria is set to send in army units ​to ‌Niger ⁠to ‌protect energy ⁠and economic interests there. And days after a foreigner was beaten to death on the streets of Durban, the stalled asylum process has left many migrants in South Africa living in fear.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Algeria to send troops to Niger in first foreign deployment in over 50 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:663ac27809dc2e126511ac29bb395b36d96a5899be8efe50cd4ef7124eb0ad11</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T10:10:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years--5abdc8f17645.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years" /><summary type="html">Algeria’s parliament on Sunday approved a resolution to send troops to Niger, making the first time Algerian soldiers will be deployed abroad since the 1973 Arab-Israeli war. Niger faces persistent attacks by armed groups, including near its border with Algeria, and the deployment comes as Algiers and Niamey are building the Trans-Saharan Gas Pipeline after decades of delays.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Building collapse in Nairobi: Search for survivors under way</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23a50deb1d36133a85ed9d26da49db2c109f6d929c1beb4cad5b2044fa049f9</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:31:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way--5d7e9d1e7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Rescuers comb through rubble in a bid to reach trapped survivors after a multi-storey building under construction in Nairobi collapses. Also, Kenya announces a second Ebola death. Earlier this week it had logged nine cases, all traced back to its first Ebola patient who died earlier this month. Finally, with the 11th edition of the iconic contemporary art festival Also Known as Africa taking place in Paris, we speak to Cape Verdean artist Amadeo Carvalho.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>SA faces rising tension as foreign national is killed amid anti-migrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43a53be89d04217fecab64e60440234a3a28e47385403d39c1e7103ea4ec7a2</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:08:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests--97fdf43717d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests" /><summary type="html">South African police are investigating the murder of a foreign national after violent protests by anti-immigrant groups swept through the central business district in Durban. The latest death follows months of violent rallies in which at least 10 foreigners were killed and several other countries on the continent raced to repatriate their people. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson.</summary></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Ivorian vinyl head's heritage hunt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:809bec7e56e246543549666c9dfbf20d948fc1550b23ff1ff9286e5b32950b4a</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:27:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt--b506a2325208.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt" /><summary type="html">This week in Across Africa: Ivorian music lover Cédric Kouamé is on a mission to restore 20th-century African vinyl and bring old-school sounds back to modern playlists. Also, 10 years after Cameroon's worst railway disaster, families are still fighting for justice for the 79 people killed. Finally, in São Tomé and Príncipe, we discover how the islands' rich volcanic soils produce some of the world's most distinctive vanilla.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Olympic fever grips Senegal as Dakar hosts Youth Olympic Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbaf4f3d54aaa94a1f17a700bd2ab1d7282ade3059699cf467ae1b4a903f2db7</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog--8929ff69c2de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog" /><summary type="html">As Senegal prepares to host the Youth Olympic Games (YOG), the first Olympic event ever organised in Africa, the country is pulling out all the stops to be ready on time. FRANCE 24’s Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Ivory Coast: Children face serious health risks from lead in paint</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4968bbc8292d1c841719860b7e67a0ad95095635b98d5dd8306a9f3b69940564</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:37:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint--1797f4fd2521.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint" /><summary type="html">Across Ivory Coast, teams are going door-to-door, testing homes for dangerous levels of lead as efforts to raise awareness of the toxic metal’s health risks intensify. Report by Jean Barrère &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa faces 'complex' Ebola outbreak after spread to Nigeria: WHO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21884371ae073b54c2ae79a7a0440e5f927af84382f736479c43529b521103cf</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who--e04938ba7420.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who" /><summary type="html">The World Health Organization warned Thursday that Africa faced a "complex" Ebola outbreak after the virus crossed from east Africa to Nigeria, marking the first case in the west of the continent.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa gripped by anti-migrant protests as foreign national is killed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f74bc625e9305b64e6e8f38e7224f088d33e4f948bf35430d1384e6ac83a13ef</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:24:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed--ea4014e7134c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed" /><summary type="html">Xenophobic unrest turns deadly in South Africa as a foreign national is beaten to death during a protest march in Durban, a city increasingly gripped by anti-migrant tensions. Meanwhile, as global efforts to raise awareness of lead poisoning intensify, teams in Ivory Coast go door-to-door testing homes for dangerous levels of the toxic metal. Finally, Ivorian authorities are cracking down on illegal mining over fears of pollution, but some young people say the activity remains one of their few sources of income.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia-Eritrea: Is there a risk of a wider conflict?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f8a4704c1e3efcc1fa5e023536e953e9c8c21e1d8052972cadcc55c22225947</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:40:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict--3f21072314d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict" /><summary type="html">Concerns are mounting as Ethiopia and Eritrea inch closer to war. With Ethiopia now having taken control of the border town of Zalambessa, the fear is that Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed will send his troops into Eritrea. In Perspective, we spoke to Martin Plaut, a senior research fellow at the Institute of Commonwealth Studies at the University of London.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Cameroon: Ten years after a massive train disaster, victims are still awaiting justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3782eac0557dde0a42fa71d38fa0d0f4421782731f70122e3e9951faf53e1f16</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:23:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice--8e557c9796f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice" /><summary type="html">It has been ten years since a Cameroon National Railway Intercity train travelling between Yaounde and Douala derailed and became the country's worst ever railway disaster. Seventy-nine people were killed and hundreds were injured. Report by Indira Ayuk, Richard Tessoh, Giresse Ngaana &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudan's war escalates as UN warns of wider regional crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6744929ec0d173284286b11f2a77c7ef341b61d747916d84f32b29f491af9cc0</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:41:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis--064ccd824912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Sudan's brutal war continues to take a devastating regional toll, as a drone strike in Abyei reportedly kills 153 people. We speak to the UN envoy for Sudan following an emergency international meeting on the escalating crisis. Also, health authorities prepare to coordinate a response as Ebola cases emerge in Nigeria and rise in Kenya. Finally, 10 years after Cameroon’s deadliest railway disaster, families of the 79 victims are still fighting for justice, saying their pain has yet to be acknowledged.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f41dfd3f14a1ecf097d09af0d0bf6a793a09ebfa4416e26f0774fa6be3e7ab6d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war--7a1f83fdb2cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war" /><summary type="html">The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Trial shows crucial role of religion in Shakahola massacre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4598cdf72b5600e2778d9c3355e51efe46cac8066e4fba6256cb3ad27ef7ec54</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:48:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre--eb311fee9b1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre" /><summary type="html">The Kenyan cult leader found guilty on Monday of the deaths of 190 children and one adult will be sentenced on November 6th. Paul Mackenzie starved his followers in what became known as the Shakahola massacre. But this trial was about more than just a criminal and his accomplices. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Bastien Renouil.</summary></entry><entry><title>South African former police chief accused of sex trafficking denied bail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66c63d2e99db378ed38e4189d77468ae64b903291665ec808104effb24c4a477</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:44:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail--532cffa65e7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail" /><summary type="html">South Africa's former deputy national commissioner, Shadrack Sibiya, has been denied bail. He is facing charges of rape, trafficking and is accused of sexually grooming a child. Investigators had argued that his accusers would be in danger if he was let out. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case amid rapid regional spread</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64eb408d71c8839b38b791febcdcff304cf70ec70e0f677ad80f4c2ddf4ac66e</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:28:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread--6d9583291599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread" /><summary type="html">After Kenya and Uganda, Nigeria has now announced its first Ebola case – a woman who was admitted to a private hospital in Abuja and travelled from Uganda. The outbreak, which originated in DR Congo in May, has been described by health officials as ​thefastest-spreading on record. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya.</summary></entry><entry><title>US sanctions on ICC are 'a shock' and 'unacceptable', Nobel peace laureate Navi Pillay says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ec62f5e576a66e3ed3212058f3539c11b8685167c269a070f6eda31a252edc4</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:11:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says--b2b2f9ec09fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Navi Pillay described the US sanctions imposed on the International Criminal Court (ICC) hours after her award as "a shock" and "unacceptable". The South African judge also defended the UN commission of inquiry she chaired which concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza: "We didn't come to that conclusion lightly." Rejecting claims that the ICC targets Africa, she said "the court is not selective".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records first Ebola case as outbreak spreads across Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bc5f86de7474612e0e31f76514e3b034410bb1c5ec831ba8d4a0291ecc3bd7b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:18:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa--ff482f120a86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has confirmed its first Ebola case in Africa's latest outbreak, while Kenya reported its ninth infection, raising fears of further spread across the continent. Africa CDC chief Jean Kaseya warned of an “extremely serious threat” and urged the international community to send funding, medical supplies and health workers.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria confirms first Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:204dc83aecdd7286b8ca3316cde930067c7a33f1263748c2a22b412f725fc217</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T21:28:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case--b377a3f657f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Nigeria confirms its first Ebola case in the midst of an outbreak that began in DR Congo in mid-May. Also, a former top South African police officer facing sexual grooming and rape charges is denied bail. Finally, São Tomé and Príncipe's rich volcanic soils produce vanilla pods with an entrancing taste unlike those grown anywhere else.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>More than 150 killed in Sudan drone strike on disputed Abyei border region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab4f71a52fde8fc05904124bd759491ac4971da4975a1fc1308c67d30674100</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:24:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region--03bda77246f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region" /><summary type="html">At least 153 people have been killed in a drone strike on a market in the disputed Abyei region, where a fire at a nearby fuel depot continued to burn on Tuesday. Local officials blamed Sudan’s military for Monday’s attack, which also left dozens injured.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ivorian DJ digs forgotten tracks, on the hunt for great classics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49fe5c65838f71f02a4075d901e2bff98468d7fc3ab608f01650da776b9f0ff9</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T13:09:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics--6c4fe973b0a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics" /><summary type="html">Cédric Kouamé travels across Ivory Coast to collect old vinyl records before restoring them. The Ivorian DJ hopes to bring national attention to his passion through an official centre dedicated to the country's historical archives, as FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exiled critic of Rwandan President Kagame found beheaded in Uganda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bd83333ff7cdb8d9b627304aa81f206ff1600d80bc1d60fa94723edc96de317</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:34:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda--41f173b50df6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda" /><summary type="html">Robert Kabera, a former Rwandan soldier living in Uganda, where he had become a vocal critic of his government back home, was found decapitated near Kampala. Rwandan authorities have been accused of assassinating opponents of President Paul Kagame. FRANCE 24's Aurore Bayoud reports from Kigali, Rwanda.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso resume dialogue with ECOWAS regional bloc</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a898134decf864717643d767092180b98728599ab0fa0b4aaf8a09526f11d5c</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:21:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc--45a34bb01829.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc" /><summary type="html">Three junta-ruled Sahel states – Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso – on Saturday resumed dialogue with the ECOWAS regional bloc, which they withdrew from more than 18 months ago. They agreed to work towards a “framework agreement” on cooperation. FRANCE 24’s regional correspondent Harold Girard tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader found guilty of murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada51ac76ce99ed7d2141cb9ef91a88500fc1874b7b5607343cad3f48a771796</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:15:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder--a2020938a17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie is convicted of 191 murders, 190 of which were of children. Also, a former Rwandan soldier and outspoken government critic, Robert Kabera, is found decapitated in Uganda. Plus we meet a young Ivorian music lover who travels around the country looking for old-school sounds that need a little TLC.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Drone attacks kill scores in Sudan's West Kordofan state and capital Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb9561bc97a57babb46daada0596779e0dde11e3ab421c1d4682e7ee32b06815</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:00:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores--3bb8acb831d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores" /><summary type="html">At least 80 people were killed in a drone strike near a market in Sudan’s southern West Kordofan state, a medical source and a witness said Monday, in one of the deadliest single attacks since the Sudan war erupted in 2023. A separate drone attack Monday in the capital Khartoum killed four, including three children.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya confirms third Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6b1d44ee8eceefbb75d404c7caa8d48c22c6fbdf01acbf91d3d57363979643</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case--716df01d45d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Kenya confirms a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from DR Congo. Also, Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in Bamenda. Finally, we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama, who digs deep into his country's colonial and industrial past to lay new creative foundations for generations to come.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry></feed>
